{"t":"read","text":"You can fit in a gulab jamun by pairing it with whole grain, dal, and vegetables to keep blood sugar steady."}
{"t":"plate","name":"Gulab jamun with balanced dinner","min":25,"items":[{"q":1,"u":"","f":"phulka"},{"q":1,"u":"katori","f":"yellow moong dal"},{"q":1,"u":"katori","f":"potol sabzi"},{"q":1,"u":"piece","f":"gulab jamun with syrup squeezed out"}],"why":"Eat the dal and sabzi before the sweet so protein and fibre slow down the rise in blood sugar.","skip":"leave the sugar syrup behind","later":"take a light ten minute stroll"}
{"t":"plate","name":"Fresh chhena and phulka dinner","min":20,"items":[{"q":2,"u":"","f":"phulka"},{"q":1,"u":"katori","f":"yellow moong dal"},{"q":1,"u":"katori","f":"potol sabzi"},{"q":2,"u":"tablespoon","f":"fresh chhena with cardamom powder"}],"why":"Fresh chhena offers sweet cardamom notes and gentle protein without the fried dough or heavy sugar syrup."}

{"t":"read","text":"Since your profile is vegetarian, we will skip the eggs and use your bread, onion, milk, and kitchen staples for an easy late breakfast."}
{"t":"plate","name":"Spiced onion bread toast with warm milk","min":15,"items":[{"q":2,"u":"slice","f":"toasted bread"},{"q":1,"u":"katori","f":"onion and tomato sauteed with spices"},{"q":1,"u":"glass","f":"warm milk"}],"why":"Warm milk gives you gentle protein, while toasted bread with sauteed onion and tomato keeps the meal comforting and quick.","skip":"Leave the eggs out to keep strictly vegetarian.","later":"Plan a protein-rich dal or khichdi for dinner."}
{"t":"plate","name":"Quick moong dal with toasted bread","min":20,"items":[{"q":2,"u":"slice","f":"lightly toasted bread"},{"q":1,"u":"katori","f":"yellow moong dal with onion"},{"q":1,"u":"glass","f":"warm milk"}],"why":"Moong dal from your staples adds solid plant protein to balance the bread and keep your energy steady till evening.","skip":"Skip eggs to align with your vegetarian preference.","later":"Have a light vegetable dinner tonight."}

{"t":"read","text":"You can easily enjoy pav bhaji tonight using raw banana instead of potato, with paneer added so the meal stays balanced."}
{"t":"plate","name":"Jain Pav Bhaji with Fresh Paneer","min":30,"items":[{"q":1.5,"u":"katori","f":"Jain bhaji made with raw banana, peas and tomato"},{"q":2,"u":"piece","f":"pav toasted with half teaspoon butter"},{"q":0.5,"u":"katori","f":"lightly pan-seared paneer cubes"},{"q":1,"u":"bowl","f":"cucumber and tomato salad with lemon"}],"why":"Raw banana gives the classic texture without root vegetables, while paneer turns a heavy street meal into a balanced dinner.","skip":"Second helpings of pav and heavy butter floating on top."}
{"t":"plate","name":"Spiced Tawa Paneer and Vegetable Mash","min":25,"items":[{"q":1.5,"u":"katori","f":"tawa mash of paneer, capsicum, peas and tomato"},{"q":2,"u":"","f":"warm phulka without ghee"},{"q":1,"u":"bowl","f":"cucumber slices with a squeeze of lemon"},{"q":1,"u":"glass","f":"plain chaas with roasted cumin"}],"why":"Delivers the same bhaji spice and warmth with whole-wheat phulka and lighter paneer for an easy digestion dinner."}

{"t":"read","text":"Since you eat vegan, we will make a rich tofu makhani curry to match the craving and lead with protein for strength."}
{"t":"plate","name":"Tofu Makhani with Phulka","min":25,"items":[{"q":1.5,"u":"katori","f":"tofu in spiced tomato cashew gravy cooked in oil"},{"q":2,"u":"","f":"phulka without ghee"},{"q":1,"u":"katori","f":"sliced cucumber and onion with lemon juice"}],"why":"Firm tofu replaces paneer for steady plant protein, cooked in a smooth tomato-cashew sauce without any dairy butter or cream.","skip":"dairy butter and dairy cream","later":"Have a light dal and vegetable bowl for dinner."}
{"t":"plate","name":"Soya Chunks and Peas Curry","min":20,"items":[{"q":1.5,"u":"katori","f":"soya chunks and peas in spiced onion tomato gravy"},{"q":1,"u":"katori","f":"steamed brown or white rice"},{"q":1,"u":"katori","f":"sliced radish and tomato"}],"why":"Soya chunks pack high protein in a familiar North Indian spiced gravy while keeping the meal easy to cook and digest."}

{"t":"read","text":"You can enjoy rajma rice today, swapping regular curd raita for a crisp lemon kachumber to keep lunch dairy-free while holding steady."}
{"t":"plate","name":"Rajma chawal with fresh kachumber","min":30,"items":[{"q":1.5,"u":"katori","f":"thick rajma curry"},{"q":1,"u":"katori","f":"steamed rice"},{"q":1,"u":"katori","f":"cucumber onion tomato kachumber with lemon"}],"why":"Rajma provides steady protein and fibre, while crisp lemon kachumber brings cooling crunch without any dairy.","skip":"Curd raita"}
{"t":"plate","name":"Lobia curry with jeera rice","min":25,"items":[{"q":1.5,"u":"katori","f":"light lobia curry"},{"q":1,"u":"katori","f":"jeera rice"},{"q":1,"u":"katori","f":"sliced cucumber and carrot with lemon juice"}],"why":"Lobia is a lighter legume cousin to rajma that cooks quickly and gives clean protein with zero dairy."}
